      "id": "bb03159d-48ce-41d4-a30e-5aefe55f0ac0",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "// numbers \n\n// different types of numbers in java\nint decimal = 100; // decimal\nint octal = 0100; // octal\nint hex = 0x100; // hexadecimal\nint binary = 0b100; // binary\n\nlong bigNumber = 1_000_000_000L; // long with underscores for readability\n\nfloat floatNumber = 3.14f; // float\ndouble doubleNumber = 3.14159; // double\n\n// float and double are used for decimal numbers, but double has more precision than float\n\n// we can also use scientific notation for very large or very small numbers\ndouble avog = 6.022E23; // Avogadro's number\ndouble planck = 6.626E-34; // Planck's constant\n",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "bb03159d-48ce-41d4-a30e-5aefe55f0ac0",
